# Using briefcase-ai

Instrument functions to capture decisions:

```python
import briefcase
briefcase.observe("console")   # "console" | "memory" | "runs.jsonl" | ExporterInstance

@briefcase.capture
def classify(text: str) -> str:
    return text.upper()
```

Rules:
- Call `briefcase.observe(...)` (or `briefcase.setup(exporter=...)`) ONCE at
  startup, or `@capture` records nothing.
- `@briefcase.capture` needs no `init()`; works on sync and async functions.
- Sanitize PII before logging/persisting:
  `from briefcase.sanitize import Sanitizer; Sanitizer().sanitize(text).sanitized`.
- Tests: `@briefcase.capture(async_capture=False)` + `briefcase.observe("memory")`
  (read `exporter.records`).
- Logging is opt-in: `briefcase.enable_logging("DEBUG")` or `BRIEFCASE_LOG_LEVEL`.
- Most features need no pip extra; only `otel`, `lakefs`, `bitemporal-iceberg`,
  `bitemporal-glue`, `kdb`, `compliance-kms`, `gym`, `evals`, `mcp` do.
